Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-26-2000||01:37 PM||||Most of you either know Bill personally or at least have read his posts on the forum.<P>Bills wife, Stormy, passed away Monday night at their home in Ohio.  Bill seems to be taking it as well as can be expected, but he needs everyones thoughts and prayers right now.  Bill asks that you pray for his 2 daughters.  They are in an unusual situation.  Bill has a personal relationship with God as did Stormy.  At least she's in a better place.  <P>Please include him and his daughters in your prayers tonight.  If you wish to send any personal thoughts, they can be forwarded through either me or Scott Haas.<P>There will be a viewing and funeral on Friday so a few extra prayers would be appreciated then to help them get through this rough time.||||reg||9
Z||000001||b lo 0||07-26-2000||01:41 PM||||I didn't know Bill; I've only been here for a week, but that is very sad news.  I will be praying for the Wilburns.  Please send them my deepest condolences.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-26-2000||01:53 PM||||I have never met Bill or Stormy but I have seen his posts on here and know that he is not far from here - I have been looking forward to meeting him.<P>It is sad indeed that he has suffered this loss and I sincerely hope that he knows that all of us here will have his daughters as well as him in our prayers.<P>My sympathy and sincerest condolences go out to him.<P>Terry||||reg||1
